  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.essepuntato.it/2008/12/pattern#Block">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">block element</rdfs:label>
    <vs:term_status rdf:resource="http://purl.org/linked-data/registry#statusStable"/>
    <skos:note xml:lang="en">
In particular, elements following this pattern can contain text and other elements compliant with the patterns `po:Inline`, `po:Atom`, `po:Milestones` and `po:Popup`. 

Furthermore, it is a requirement that block elements are contained only by container and popup elements.
    </skos:note>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="n27f50dd15b7c417789d400bde3c61873b91"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An element that organises the document content as a sequence of nestable elements and text nodes.</rdfs:comment>
    <vann:example>
        :my-paragraph a po:Block ;
                po:isContainedBy :my-section ;
                po:contains :my-span .
        </vann:example>
    <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="http://www.essepuntato.it/2008/12/pattern#Inline"/>
